


# Overview

# This project shows how to build a containerized HR data analytics pipeline
# using Docker and Python. The idea is simple:
# put all the data analysis logic into a Python script,
# containerize it with Docker, and make it reproducible anywhere.
# It’s a great example of combining data analytics with DevOps tools.
#Note: need to look at it again
#Note 2 : update Docker




# Key Features

# Cleans and transforms HR data automatically.
# Calculates key HR insights like Attrition Rate and Average Salary.
# Builds department-level summaries (headcount, salary, tenure, etc.).
# Correlates engagement, tenure, and performance metrics.
# Uses Docker so the entire pipeline runs the same everywhere.





# Tech Stack

# Python 3.10       -- For analytics and data handling
# Pandas, NumPy     -- For data manipulation and statistics
# Scikit-learn      -- For basic feature engineering (if needed)
# Docker            -- To containerize and run everything consistently





# How to Run the Project


# Clone this repository
# This copies the project to your computer.
#```bash
#git clone https://github.com/MS8642/HR_Docker_Analytics.git
#cd HR_Docker_Analytics


# Build the docker image
# docker build -t hr-analysis .

# Run the container
# docker run --rm hr-analysis

#You will see the information about the HR dataset I used.

#Dataset used from Kaggle : https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/rhuebner/human-resources-data-set?resource=download

